Use case: stylized-concept. Production game sprite sheet on a truly transparent background: EXACTLY FOUR isolated stone steles in ONE horizontal row, evenly spaced, very generous transparent gutters in every cell, nothing touching a cell edge. No text, numbers, labels, arrows, floor, ground shadow, backdrops or UI. Flat sprite sheet, not a mockup, no perspective convergence.
All four share the SAME squat standing stone block: a broad low tapered slab, nearly square front face reading at 28x28 logical pixels but drawn LARGE in the cell, slightly wider at the foot, chipped worn edges, cold blue-grey slate with faint violet vein, thin dark teal moss along the base, two tiny pale flowers at the foot. Front-facing orthographic with a small visible top face, crisp painterly pixel clusters, soft light from the upper left, restrained highlights. Same silhouette, size, baseline, facing, lighting and scale for all four; ONLY the carved glyph differs.
Each stele carries ONE SMALL glyph cut into the front face and filled with dim old honey brass. The glyph is compact and sits in the middle of the face, occupying only about 40 percent of the face width, with a wide blank border of bare stone all around it; it must never touch the edges of the stone, because a brass ring will later be fitted over the face around it. Same thin even stroke weight in all four, shallow engraving catching light on its lower edge, NO glow outside the stone, NO other markings:
cell 1 CRESCENT MOON tilted about 30 degrees, horns opening to the upper right;
cell 2 a POINTED LEAF seen flat, a single centre vein, tip up;
cell 3 an EIGHT-POINTED STAR, four long points on the axes and four short between them;
cell 4 a single WATER DROPLET with a round belly and sharp top, one short ripple line beneath.
The four glyphs must look like one family carved by the same hand: same stroke width, same engraving depth, same wear. Keep the stone quiet and matte so the glyph stays the only identifier. Objects fully inside their cells.

Use case: stylized-concept. Production game sprite sheet on a truly transparent background: EXACTLY FOUR isolated receiving mouths in ONE horizontal row, evenly spaced, generous transparent gutters, nothing touching a cell edge. No text, numbers, labels, arrows, floor or UI.
Each mouth is a small RECESSED SOCKET IN THE FOREST FLOOR, reading at 12x12 logical pixels but drawn large: a shallow square-ish stone inset with a dark slate lip, its interior almost black, a hairline brass seam around the rim, tiny chips and one blade of moss. These are DARK MARKS: they must stay almost illegible in full light and only reveal their information when no lantern light falls on them. Do NOT paint a glow, halo or bright rim.
Inside each socket, TWO OR THREE TINY WARM FIREFLY DOTS are perched at the rim, and their POSITION is the only signal, pointing along one of three directions (north, south-east, south-west):
cell 1 dots clustered at the SOUTH-WEST edge;
cell 2 dots clustered at the NORTH edge;
cell 3 dots clustered at the NORTH edge;
cell 4 dots clustered at the SOUTH-WEST edge.
The dots are 1-pixel warm amber specks with the faintest one-pixel falloff, never a large bloom. All four sockets share the same stone, size, depth and lighting; only the dot direction differs. Front-facing orthographic, crisp painterly pixel clusters, desaturated cold palette so the amber dots are the only warm accent.
